-- הסכם קיבוצי — מדריכי של"ח (נחתם 11.77, נרשם 15.3.1978): the special
-- collective agreement between the Government and the national committee
-- of Shelah teachers with the Civil Service Union, for the teaching
-- employees who work as Shelah guides in post-primary schools, registered
-- on 15.3.1978 (no. 31/78), in force from 1.9.1977. Its body is short —
-- the preamble, earlier terms, the annexed regulations, industrial peace,
-- its start and scope, registration, publication and extension — and its
-- annex, "תקנון עבודת מדריכי של"ח", sets the guides' duties, rights and
-- grades.
--
-- The takanon's §6.17 restates the annex, most of it in the same words or
-- nearly, and its rules were encoded there first
-- (l4/takanon/takanon-sherut-ovdei-horaa/6.17.l4). So each row of the
-- annex the takanon prints in the same or nearly the same words is cited
-- "as in the takanon's §6.17", by the rule that encodes it there, and this
-- file imports it; what the takanon has since changed — the pay for an
-- overnight activity, updated there on 6.8.03 — and what it does not
-- restate are encoded here as the agreement of 1978 sets them. The scan
-- has words the corpus cannot read ([לא קריא]); a rule that turns on one
-- takes it as an input.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT `takanon-6-17`
IMPORT wage_protection_law

§ `הסכם קיבוצי — מדריכי של"ח (1977–1978)`

§§ `המבוא`

-- akn:preamble/p1 A file mark (barcode 07154); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p2 The Registrar's stamp: registered on 15 March 1978, number 31/78; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p3 akn:preamble/p4 The agreement's title, made and signed in Jerusalem in November 1977 (the day struck out and illegible); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9 akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11 akn:preamble/p12 The parties: the Government ("side A"), and the national committee of Shelah teachers and the Civil Service Union, together and each alone ("side B"); no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p13 akn:preamble/p14 A recital: an agreement for the teaching employees employed as Shelah guides in post-primary schools ("מדריכי של"ח").
-- akn:preamble/p15 akn:preamble/p16 A recital that the parties agreed what follows, and the words of agreement; no rule.

`what the Shelah agreement of 1978 lacks` MEANS
    LIST `the text is missing` "מילים שהסריקה אינה קוראת ([לא קריא]): בין היתר מספר ימי מפעל השירות הלאומי (נספח, 3(א)(5), 3(ב)(4), 5(ב)), שנות תקופת הניסיון (4(א)(1)–(2)), שעות יום שדה (5(א)) וסעיף 5(ה) על הוותק המקצועי",
         `outside the corpus` "חוזר המנהל הכללי שבו פורסם ההסכם, ונוהל פעולות הגדנ\"ע"

§§ `1 המבוא`

-- §1: the preamble is a part of the agreement, its provisions as if they
-- were in one of its sections.
@ref akn:art_1/p1
`the preamble of the Shelah agreement of 1978 is part of it` MEANS TRUE

§§ `2 תנאים קודמים`

-- §2: every term agreed in writing between the sides on the eve of the
-- signing goes on applying in the agreement's term, unless and so far as
-- this agreement changes it expressly.
@ref akn:art_2/p1
`earlier terms stand after the Shelah agreement of 1978 unless changed expressly` MEANS TRUE

§§ `3 התקנון`

-- §3: the regulations for the guides' work, annexed, are part of the
-- agreement and apply to the guides.
@ref akn:art_3/p1
`the annexed regulations of 1978 bind the Shelah guides` MEANS TRUE

§§ `4 שקט תעשייתי`

DECLARE `Shelah action of 1978` IS ONE OF
    `strike over a matter the Shelah agreement of 1978 settles`
    `see that its members keep the Shelah agreement of 1978`
    `register the Shelah agreement of 1978 as a special collective agreement`
    `publish the Shelah agreement of 1978 in the director-general's circular`
    `bring the joining letters to the owners for signature`
    `confirm in writing that the guide has started work`
    `discuss the guides' training toward certification`

-- (א): in the agreement's term no side, its members or units, strikes or
-- [illegible] against the other over a matter it settles; a "strike" is an
-- organised stoppage, whole or partial, of a group of guides, a slowdown
-- and other organised disruption among it. (ב): each side does its best
-- that its members keep the agreement.
-- not weighed against `the Advance Notice Law`: "הפסקת עבודה" in 4(א) is an
-- organised stoppage, the strike the parties forgo, and "חודש ימים מראש" in
-- the annex (3(א)(13), 3(ב)(11)) is a month's notice of a demand to instruct
-- at a seminar; neither is notice of a dismissal or a resignation.
@ref akn:art_4__para_a akn:art_4__para_b
`industrial peace of the Shelah agreement of 1978` MEANS
    PARTY `the teachers' union`
    SHANT `strike over a matter the Shelah agreement of 1978 settles`

`each side sees that its members keep the Shelah agreement of 1978` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `see that its members keep the Shelah agreement of 1978`

§§ `5 תחולה`

-- (א): in force from י"ח באלול תשל"ז, 1.9.1977.
@ref akn:art_5__para_a
`the Shelah agreement of 1978 is in force from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 1977

-- (ב) is restated in the takanon's §6.17.1 (below). (ג): subject to (א)
-- and (ב), it applies to the guides employed on the day it was signed and
-- to their work in its term, and to those who worked as guides in its term
-- and retired by the signing; not to a guide dismissed before it for a
-- disciplinary or a criminal offence.
@ref akn:art_5__para_c
GIVEN `employed on the signing, or worked as a guide in its term and retired by it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `dismissed before the signing for a disciplinary or criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Shelah agreement of 1978 reaches the guide` `employed on the signing, or worked as a guide in its term and retired by it` `dismissed before the signing for a disciplinary or criminal offence` IF
    `employed on the signing, or worked as a guide in its term and retired by it`
    AND NOT `dismissed before the signing for a disciplinary or criminal offence`

#ASSERT NOT `the Shelah agreement of 1978 reaches the guide` TRUE TRUE

-- (א) of the second list: registered as a special collective agreement
-- under the Collective Agreements Law, 1957; (ב): published in the
-- director-general's circular; (ג): to extend it to every other owner and
-- guide, the sides' signatures are a joining letter under §8(2) of that law
-- by the other owners, the joining letters brought to the owners, the
-- committee and the union to sign later.
@ref akn:art_5__hc_1__para_a akn:art_5__hc_1__para_b akn:art_5__hc_1__para_c
`registering and publishing the Shelah agreement of 1978` MEANS
    PARTY `the State`
    MUST  `register the Shelah agreement of 1978 as a special collective agreement`
    HENCE (PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
           MUST  `publish the Shelah agreement of 1978 in the director-general's circular`
           HENCE (PARTY `the State`
                  MUST  `bring the joining letters to the owners for signature`))

-- akn:conclusions/p1 akn:conclusions/p2 akn:conclusions/t1 akn:conclusions/p3 The signing formula, the sides and the signatures; no rule.

§§ `נספח — תקנון עבודת מדריכי של"ח`

-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 akn:att_1__hc_1/p2 The annex's title, "the regulations of the Shelah guides' work", and the section of the agreement it belongs to (the number illegible); no rule.

-- 1: the provisions for teaching employees in primary schools apply to the
-- guides too, unless and so far as a provision says otherwise.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_1/p1
`the primary-school provisions apply to a Shelah guide unless the regulations of 1978 say otherwise` MEANS TRUE

-- akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4/p1 The words "a Shelah guide is entitled —" that open the list of 4.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_a The words of 4(א) that open its two cases of tenure, encoded with them below.

-- 4(ב): to sit supplementary exams and reach the grade of a certified guide
-- by the addendum's rules (below).
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_b
`a Shelah guide may sit supplementary exams toward certification, by the 1978 addendum` MEANS TRUE

-- 4(ג): for a special activity with a night out, (1) one from outside (a
-- substitute up to 51 days): a certified guide's monthly salary at the
-- first grade and seniority (the minimum), over 120, times his hours worked
-- (at most 10), plus 24% for social rights; (2) a regular guide, for the
-- hours beyond the day — 11 less the hours the school's roster owes that
-- day — his monthly salary by grade and seniority over 120, times those
-- hours, plus 24%. (The takanon's §6.17.7 has updated both since: a senior
-- guide's third year for the first, 14 hours for the second.)
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_c akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_c__cls_1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_c__cls_1/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_c__cls_1/p3 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_c__cls_2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_c__cls_2/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_c__cls_2/p3
GIVEN `a certified guide's minimum monthly salary` IS A NUMBER, `hours worked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `an outside worker's pay for a night out, by 1978` `a certified guide's minimum monthly salary` `hours worked` IS
    `a certified guide's minimum monthly salary` DIVIDED BY 120 TIMES (min `hours worked` 10) TIMES (1 PLUS 24%)

GIVEN `his monthly salary` IS A NUMBER, `hours owed that day by the roster` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a regular guide's pay for a night out, by 1978` `his monthly salary` `hours owed that day by the roster` IS
    `his monthly salary` DIVIDED BY 120 TIMES (max (11 MINUS `hours owed that day by the roster`) 0) TIMES (1 PLUS 24%)

#ASSERT `an outside worker's pay for a night out, by 1978` 1200 12 EQUALS 124
#ASSERT `a regular guide's pay for a night out, by 1978` 1200 5 EQUALS 74.4

-- 4(ד): for a special activity without a night out (escorting pupils to
-- bases among it), pay for the hours worked, at most 10 a day, less the
-- hours the roster owes that day; a field day is not a special activity.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_d
GIVEN `hours worked` IS A NUMBER, `hours owed that day by the roster` IS A NUMBER, `is a field day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours paid for a day activity, by 1978` `hours worked` `hours owed that day by the roster` `is a field day` IS
    IF `is a field day`
    THEN 0
    ELSE max ((min `hours worked` 10) MINUS `hours owed that day by the roster`) 0

#ASSERT `hours paid for a day activity, by 1978` 12 4 FALSE EQUALS 6

-- 4(ו): for the preparation of 3(א)(2) or 3(ב)(2), pay worth an hour's work.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_f
`the hours paid for preparing a field day, by 1978` MEANS 1

-- 4(ז): pay for 12 hours' work on a Sabbath in national service, with the
-- pay for work on the weekly rest day under the Hours of Work and Rest
-- Law (its year illegible here; l4/laws/hours-of-work-law.l4).
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_g
`the hours paid for a Sabbath of national service, by 1978` MEANS 12

-- 4(ח): on starting work, the teaching personnel division's written
-- confirmation that he has started.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_h
`confirming a guide's start, by 1978` MEANS
    PARTY `the teaching personnel division`
    MUST  `confirm in writing that the guide has started work`

-- 4(יג): leave by the calendar of recesses of the high schools the Ministry
-- recognises (outside the corpus).
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_jc
`a Shelah guide's leave follows the high schools' calendar, by 1978` MEANS TRUE

-- The Annual Leave Law, as in the takanon's §6.17 (imported): 4(יג) gives
-- the guide the high schools' recesses, and 3(א)(9) and 3(ב)(8) let the
-- supervision's enterprises take no more than 5 days of them, the rule the
-- takanon restates; a full year's summer less those days is more than §3's
-- 28. The floor is met, on the takanon's rule.
#ASSERT `the Shelach guide's summer, less the enterprise days, meets section 3 of the Annual Leave Law`

-- 4(יד): equipment, for a full position, as the Ministry decides: (1) two
-- suits (shirt and trousers) of dacron cloth in khaki-like shades the
-- supervision and the committee agree; (2) a rainproof windbreaker of those
-- shades, every three years; (3) paratrooper boots of the army's quality.
-- 4(טו): for a part position, in whole or in part, by its share.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_jd akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_jd__cls_1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_jd__cls_2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_jd__cls_3 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4__subpara_if
`the suits a full-position guide is given, by 1978` MEANS 2
`the years between windbreakers, by 1978` MEANS 3

GIVEN `the full position's equipment` IS A NUMBER, `the position share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a part-position guide's equipment, by 1978` `the full position's equipment` `the position share` IS
    `the full position's equipment` TIMES (min `the position share` 1)

-- 5(ב): the national-service project lasts up to [illegible] days, where
-- the supervision decides. 5(ג): the supervision sets the composition of
-- the guide's position on his starting and may change it during the year
-- without lessening its size.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5__subpara_b akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5__subpara_c
GIVEN `the size before` IS A NUMBER, `the size after` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a change of the position's composition keeps its size, by 1978` `the size before` `the size after` IF
    `the size after` AT LEAST `the size before`

-- 5(ה): of the guides' recognised professional seniority (the paragraph is
-- mostly illegible in the scan; `what the Shelah agreement of 1978 lacks`).
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5__subpara_e
`5(ה) of 1978 is legible` MEANS FALSE

-- 5(ו): the content of the guides' training [illegible] the supervision;
-- its aims, (1) to bring the guides to certification, (2) training for
-- certified guides. 5(ט): a special committee of the Ministry and the
-- committee discusses the guides' training toward certification, with
-- proposals by the end of February 1978.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5__subpara_f akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5__subpara_f__cls_1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5__subpara_f__cls_2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5__subpara_i
`discussing the guides' certification, by 1978` MEANS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `discuss the guides' training toward certification`

`the committee's proposals are due by, by 1978` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 1978

-- 5(ז): the guide answers personally for the equipment handed him; lost
-- [illegible], he returns equipment of [illegible] value or its value in
-- money as the supervision assesses it; on appeal, the coordinating
-- supervisor sets up a parity committee whose decision is final. The sum is
-- the guide's debt to the State, which the Ministry may deduct from his
-- salary and any other sum the Government owes him "בכפיפות לחוק הגנת
-- השכר תשי"ח-1958" — the same words the takanon's §6.17.3(ו) restates.
-- What the law leaves of the deduction from his salary in a month (§25): a
-- debt under the guide's written undertaking, at most a quarter of the
-- month's wage (§25(א)(6)); from his last wage, the whole balance (§25(ב));
-- without either, nothing from his salary. Against the Wage Protection Law
-- (MMS-601), it meets the floor.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5__subpara_g
GIVEN `the debt` IS A NUMBER
      `the month's wage` IS A NUMBER
      `he undertook the debt in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is his last wage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the debt the 1978 regulations deduct from a month's salary` `the debt` `the month's wage` `he undertook the debt in writing` `it is his last wage` IS
    IF `it is his last wage`
    THEN `what section 25(ב) lets be deducted from the last wage` TRUE `the debt` `the month's wage`
    ELSE IF `he undertook the debt in writing`
         THEN min `the debt` (`the most section 25(א)(6) lets be deducted in a month` `the month's wage`)
         ELSE 0

#ASSERT `the debt the 1978 regulations deduct from a month's salary` 4000 10000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 2500
#ASSERT `the debt the 1978 regulations deduct from a month's salary` 4000 10000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the debt the 1978 regulations deduct from a month's salary` 4000 10000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 4000
#ASSERT `the debt the 1978 regulations deduct from a month's salary` 4000 10000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the debt 6.17.3ו deducts from a month's salary` 4000 10000 TRUE FALSE

-- 5(ח)(5): a guide who moves to teaching keeps the continuity of the
-- rights gathered from his start as a guide, seniority among them (the
-- rest of the paragraph is illegible).
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5__subpara_h__cls_5
`a guide who moves to teaching keeps his seniority, by 1978` MEANS TRUE

-- The addendum's headings, and its rows the takanon does not restate in
-- the same words: a "certified guide" is (1) one with a matriculation
-- certificate who passed the guides' seminar and the exams in "Shelah and
-- its teaching", psychology and Hebrew, with a positive evaluation after at
-- least [illegible] year (2, a guide of 10–11 years' schooling, is restated
-- below); a guide "of stage א"א" passes one exam in "Shelah and its
-- teaching" [the rest illegible]; an uncertified guide of stage א' is (1)
-- one with an Israeli matriculation certificate the Ministry recognises,
-- (2)–(4) restated below; one of stage ב', any guide not in those.
@ref akn:att_1__hc_1__hc_1__para_a akn:att_1__hc_1__hc_1__para_b akn:att_1__hc_1__hc_1__para_b/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1 akn:att_1__hc_1__hc_1__para_c akn:att_1__hc_1__hc_1__para_c/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1__hc_1__para_d akn:att_1__hc_1__hc_1__para_d__subpara_1 akn:att_1__hc_1__hc_1__para_e
DECLARE `Shelah guide grade of 1978` IS ONE OF
    `a certified Shelah guide, of 1978`
    `a Shelah guide of stage א"א, of 1978`
    `an uncertified Shelah guide of stage א', of 1978`
    `an uncertified Shelah guide of stage ב', of 1978`

GIVEN `matriculation, the seminar and the three exams, with a positive evaluation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `passed the exam in Shelah and its teaching, as stage א"א asks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a recognised Israeli matriculation, or (2)–(4)'s schooling and exams` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Shelah guide grade of 1978`
DECIDE `the Shelah guide's grade, by 1978` `matriculation, the seminar and the three exams, with a positive evaluation` `passed the exam in Shelah and its teaching, as stage א"א asks` `a recognised Israeli matriculation, or (2)–(4)'s schooling and exams` IS
    IF `matriculation, the seminar and the three exams, with a positive evaluation` THEN `a certified Shelah guide, of 1978`
    ELSE IF `passed the exam in Shelah and its teaching, as stage א"א asks` THEN `a Shelah guide of stage א"א, of 1978`
         ELSE IF `a recognised Israeli matriculation, or (2)–(4)'s schooling and exams` THEN `an uncertified Shelah guide of stage א', of 1978`
              ELSE `an uncertified Shelah guide of stage ב', of 1978`

#ASSERT `the Shelah guide's grade, by 1978` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `an uncertified Shelah guide of stage ב', of 1978`

